      "title": "Handle invalid subprocess arguments after journaling",
      "description": "`launch()` converts `OSError` from `Popen` into a recorded `LaunchError`, but `Popen` can also raise `ValueError` for arguments or a working directory containing an embedded NUL. `_launch()` has already committed the journal entry before calling `launch()`, so that exception escapes and leaves the entry unresolved rather than recording the launch failure. Validate these values before journaling or handle this launch failure so the entry can be resolved.",
